WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.941 --> 00:00:07.911
♪♪

00:00:08.045 --> 00:00:09.346
&gt;&gt;&gt; We're following several new

00:00:09.413 --> 00:00:11.348
developments this morning out of

00:00:11.348 --> 00:00:11.415
Russia.

00:00:11.548 --> 00:00:12.249
President Vladimir Putin just

00:00:12.382 --> 00:00:14.151
moments ago addressing law

00:00:14.284 --> 00:00:15.385
enforcement involved in this

00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:17.454
weekend's armed rebellion by the

00:00:17.587 --> 00:00:18.555
Wagner mercenary group telling

00:00:18.689 --> 00:00:20.123
the troops that they, quote,

00:00:20.257 --> 00:00:21.358
stopped a civil war.

00:00:21.358 --> 00:00:22.759
Russia also announced it is

00:00:22.893 --> 00:00:24.461
dropping charges against the

00:00:24.594 --> 00:00:26.363
Wagner group and its leader

00:00:26.496 --> 00:00:28.298
yevgeniy prigozhin and the

00:00:28.432 --> 00:00:30.367
mercenaries are preparing to

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:31.034
hand over heavy military

00:00:31.368 --> 00:00:32.769
equipment to Russian troops.

00:00:32.903 --> 00:00:35.005
Joining us now is bill brouder,

00:00:35.372 --> 00:00:36.173
once the largest foreign

00:00:36.306 --> 00:00:38.375
investor in Russia and now one

00:00:38.508 --> 00:00:41.378
of the Kremlin and president

00:00:41.378 --> 00:00:43.914
Putin's significant enemies.

00:00:44.047 --> 00:00:47.050
He singled him out in 2018.

00:00:47.384 --> 00:00:48.852
He is also the author of

00:00:48.986 --> 00:00:50.754
"Freezing order" true story of

00:00:50.887 --> 00:00:52.723
money laundering murder and

00:00:52.856 --> 00:00:53.423
surviving Vladimir Putin's

00:00:53.557 --> 00:00:53.790
wrath.

00:00:53.924 --> 00:00:54.691
Bill, thank you so much for

00:00:54.825 --> 00:00:55.425
joining us.

00:00:55.559 --> 00:00:56.994
I think I actually want to start

00:00:57.394 --> 00:00:58.295
there because throughout the

00:00:58.428 --> 00:01:00.731
course of this weekend and in

00:01:00.864 --> 00:01:03.000
the days since, I have

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.534
constantly wondered when is the

00:01:04.668 --> 00:01:06.103
crack down happening.

00:01:06.236 --> 00:01:08.205
There's no way that yevgeniy

00:01:08.338 --> 00:01:09.606
prigozhin can be allowed to just

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.676
go to Belarus or go to Africa or

00:01:12.809 --> 00:01:13.910
wherever he might want to go.

00:01:14.044 --> 00:01:15.979
That seems like an

00:01:16.113 --> 00:01:16.813
inevitability.

00:01:16.947 --> 00:01:17.781
Is it?

00:01:17.914 --> 00:01:19.816
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:21.418
Basically Putin can't stand --

00:01:21.418 --> 00:01:24.488
he can't tolerate being

00:01:24.621 --> 00:01:24.921
disrespected.

00:01:25.055 --> 00:01:26.590
This is -- the psychology of

00:01:26.723 --> 00:01:27.891
Russian leadership is like the

00:01:28.025 --> 00:01:29.426
psychology of a prison yard.

00:01:29.459 --> 00:01:31.428
In order for Putin to have been

00:01:31.428 --> 00:01:34.398
the leader for 23 years, he's

00:01:34.531 --> 00:01:36.767
had to be the -- seem to be the

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.101
meanest guy in the prison yard

00:01:38.235 --> 00:01:40.871
the one that would cause damage

00:01:41.004 --> 00:01:41.571
to anybody who even looked at

00:01:41.705 --> 00:01:42.539
him the wrong way.

00:01:42.672 --> 00:01:44.174
And yevgeniy prigozhin didn't

00:01:44.307 --> 00:01:45.876
just look at him the wrong way,

00:01:46.009 --> 00:01:48.145
he disrespected him in the most

00:01:48.278 --> 00:01:50.147
massive, humiliating way.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:51.581
It's not just a question of what

00:01:51.715 --> 00:01:53.116
happens to prigozhin but what

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:56.086
happens to all the other people

00:01:56.219 --> 00:01:58.355
who either didn't immediately

00:01:58.488 --> 00:02:00.357
declare loyalty to Putin during

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:03.727
that day or who kept quiet or

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.495
who perhaps were even working on

00:02:05.629 --> 00:02:06.263
the other side.

00:02:06.396 --> 00:02:09.599
In my opinion, the only way that

00:02:09.733 --> 00:02:11.468
Putin can stay in power is for

00:02:11.468 --> 00:02:13.770
him to reassert his authority

00:02:13.904 --> 00:02:16.373
and the only way he can do that

00:02:16.506 --> 00:02:18.608
is to become extremely

00:02:18.742 --> 00:02:19.643
aggressive, dangerous and

00:02:19.776 --> 00:02:21.478
violent towards all sorts of

00:02:21.478 --> 00:02:22.212
people who he doesn't believe

00:02:22.345 --> 00:02:23.080
are loyal to him.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.714
I think there's going to be a

00:02:24.848 --> 00:02:26.383
huge sort of purge, crackdown,

00:02:26.516 --> 00:02:28.552
whatever you want to call it, of

00:02:28.685 --> 00:02:31.588
the elite, of the government, of

00:02:31.721 --> 00:02:33.056
the military and of the

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:34.891
oligarchs for Putin to

00:02:35.025 --> 00:02:36.593
reestablish his authority.

00:02:36.726 --> 00:02:38.195
&gt;&gt; We saw prigozhin but we

00:02:38.328 --> 00:02:40.163
haven't seen any of the inner

00:02:40.297 --> 00:02:41.665
circle or close advisers to

00:02:41.798 --> 00:02:44.901
president Putin side with

00:02:45.035 --> 00:02:46.603
prigozhin or speak out of turn

00:02:46.736 --> 00:02:47.504
at some point.

00:02:47.504 --> 00:02:48.605
Why would this be a threat to

00:02:48.738 --> 00:02:50.240
his power if no one else is

00:02:50.373 --> 00:02:51.508
standing up right now.

00:02:51.508 --> 00:02:52.742
&gt;&gt; Well, because the only reason

00:02:52.876 --> 00:02:54.044
that Putin has been able to stay

00:02:54.177 --> 00:02:56.246
in power is that everyone is

00:02:56.379 --> 00:02:56.847
scared of him.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:59.149
And what this showed is that you

00:02:59.516 --> 00:03:00.984
can basically -- a group of I

00:03:01.118 --> 00:03:02.452
think it was 8,000 men could

00:03:02.586 --> 00:03:06.490
drive along the highway and take

00:03:06.623 --> 00:03:09.759
over rostov, a major military

00:03:09.893 --> 00:03:11.795
base and drive to the next town

00:03:11.928 --> 00:03:13.163
and nobody said anything.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:14.464
The people took selfies with

00:03:14.598 --> 00:03:18.335
them and hugged them.

00:03:18.468 --> 00:03:23.540
And so if Putin can't exert his

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:25.208
power by just existing, then all

00:03:25.542 --> 00:03:26.409
of a sudden other people will

00:03:26.543 --> 00:03:28.145
say, look, this is a very

00:03:28.278 --> 00:03:29.546
profitable job to have to be the

00:03:29.579 --> 00:03:30.447
president of Russia.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:31.848
You can get hundreds of billions

00:03:31.982 --> 00:03:33.550
of dollars if you do this job.

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:34.918
There's a huge incentive for

00:03:35.051 --> 00:03:36.820
anybody to have a go at him.

00:03:36.953 --> 00:03:38.622
It looks like he's weak, they

00:03:38.755 --> 00:03:39.556
will have a go.

00:03:39.556 --> 00:03:41.892
That is the -- it's the

00:03:42.025 --> 00:03:43.560
psychology of a prison yard

00:03:43.627 --> 00:03:45.662
there where, you know, unless he

00:03:45.795 --> 00:03:47.564
can become -- he can be seen

00:03:47.564 --> 00:03:49.199
again as the scariest, most

00:03:49.566 --> 00:03:51.568
brutal guy, his days are

00:03:51.568 --> 00:03:52.636
numbered.

00:03:52.769 --> 00:03:54.738
&gt;&gt; I was struck yesterday former

00:03:54.871 --> 00:03:56.740
ambassador John Bolton told my

00:03:56.873 --> 00:04:00.010
colleague poppy, don't

00:04:00.143 --> 00:04:00.710
underestimate the possibility

00:04:00.844 --> 00:04:01.578
that Putin could turn this to

00:04:01.578 --> 00:04:02.112
his advantage.

00:04:02.245 --> 00:04:03.580
Do you think that's overstating

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.782
his 23 years of ability to do

00:04:05.916 --> 00:04:06.983
such things given what we saw

00:04:07.117 --> 00:04:09.586
over the course of the last four

00:04:09.586 --> 00:04:09.653
days?

00:04:09.786 --> 00:04:12.822
&gt;&gt; Well, what I know about Putin

00:04:12.956 --> 00:04:15.892
is that he is slow to react to

00:04:16.026 --> 00:04:16.226
things.

00:04:16.359 --> 00:04:17.794
Stuff happens and then, you

00:04:17.928 --> 00:04:19.629
know, a day, a week, a month

00:04:19.763 --> 00:04:21.631
might go by, but I guarantee you

00:04:21.765 --> 00:04:23.200
that Putin is now sitting there

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.869
saying, okay, how do we get

00:04:26.002 --> 00:04:27.204
control over the situation?

00:04:27.604 --> 00:04:30.140
He can use the situation to

00:04:30.273 --> 00:04:32.242
organize and justify a massive

00:04:32.375 --> 00:04:32.609
crackdown.

00:04:32.742 --> 00:04:33.643
And it wouldn't be unusual.

00:04:33.777 --> 00:04:36.580
We saw the same thing with

00:04:36.713 --> 00:04:38.648
erdogan in Turkey, coup attempt

00:04:38.782 --> 00:04:39.616
made against him.

00:04:39.716 --> 00:04:42.252
He arrested everybody in sight.

00:04:42.385 --> 00:04:43.753
Literally 50,000 people went to

00:04:43.887 --> 00:04:45.622
jail in Turkey.

00:04:45.622 --> 00:04:47.290
People he didn't trust.

00:04:47.624 --> 00:04:48.592
And I'm almost certain that

00:04:48.725 --> 00:04:49.626
Putin will do that.

00:04:49.759 --> 00:04:53.263
If he does do that, if he takes

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:57.167
this coup as his -- as a sort of

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:58.635
impetus to even crack down

00:04:58.768 --> 00:05:01.638
further, then he may very well

00:05:01.638 --> 00:05:03.640
end up more control over the

00:05:03.673 --> 00:05:05.041
Russian situation than he had

00:05:05.175 --> 00:05:05.642
before.

00:05:05.642 --> 00:05:06.910
It could also go the other way.

00:05:07.043 --> 00:05:08.478
That's why we're in this period

00:05:08.612 --> 00:05:10.146
of really dramatic uncertainty.

